Z||000013||Zoom88||12-01-2001||01:13 AM|||| Another Kudo for the scoops, The wife and I went cruising this evening (first time since adding the scoops) She made a comment on how many people where noticing the car. Here is the kicker, she suggested I might want to add an alarm system......hehe, she doesn't know I have been wanting to do this myself, put the icing on the cake when it was her suggestion...big grin....I just played along<BR> "do you really think I need one"? Well, if you think I should, I guess I will go ahead and install one .  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000014||Oreif||12-01-2001||01:16 AM||||As usual those look GREAT. Now everyone can see what they look like on a car without aero-molding. I bought one of the first sets and they are awesome for quality. Many others require you to cut/drill the holes and do all the finishing work. But these ARE READY TO PAINT. I had mine painted at a friends Body shop and they were impressed by the high quality of the panels. <BR> By the way The forum member who sells them is 007DOUG, The forum member who actually makes them is SAGE.<BR>They are both excellent folks to do business with.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000015||Zoom88||12-01-2001||01:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Damn that is one clean Formula! Those scoops look great! I really like the way the tires look also, they look good. That car is primo! A+++</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thank You, I appreciate the comments...it took allot of honey do's before I could talk the wife into letting me purchase them....Of course now that they are on it was all her idea !!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000016||carpetviper||12-01-2001||06:14 PM||||Those scoops look great! I wasn't sure how they'd look on my '86 SE, but you've convinced me. I'm asking for the scoops for christmas.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||avengador1||12-01-2001||07:03 PM||||I too think I am going to get those as they seem to require the least amount of work before you can use them. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||Sage||12-01-2001||07:54 PM||||Terry,<P>Your car is GORGEOUS! Can't remember seeing a nicer looking formula anytime, anywhere.  <P>Looks like you did an excellent job with the finishing and paint on the scoops.  They look very nice on there, even if I do say so myself.  Course you did the hard work, putting them on there, LOL.  <P>You must have a great wife too!<P>Thanks for showing us your ride and showing off the scoops too.<P>Like to remind anyone thinking about getting these, there normally is no "on hand supply" of these things.  Because of the cost of production, they are made to order.  In other words, they aren't made without an order.  We tell folks to expect a 6 - 8 week wait, but it usually doesn't take that long, we just like to prepare people and give ourselves ample time to do the job right.  Eventually we WILL get to the point that we have a small supply on hand, but we're not there yet.  Right now I have one set that could be ready to go in a days time.  I will be making a few sets in the next couple weeks, but do have some other projects in the works.  Just a little FYI.<P>Good job on the scoops, and you are a good photographer too!  Those are some nice pics.<P>Keep up the good work.<P>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000019||fropuff||12-01-2001||08:16 PM||||Looks nice!  You have a damn nice car as well.  I was wondering about the paint.. I was wondering how much you used to paint the two scoops.  Reason I'm asking is that I need to repaint the right fender, front bumper, and rear bumper on my '92 Grand Prix.  I was wondering how much I would need.  I was thinking two cans, but it may need three?  I would only do around three coats, so it's not as many coats as you used.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Toogy||12-01-2001||08:19 PM||||I was just wondering if you had your car lowered at all?||||reg||1
Z||000021||Zoom88||12-01-2001||08:23 PM||||Thanks everyone, your comments make it all worth while. I love taking pictures of the car also, have some pics of the interior if anyone is interested I'll post a few. Like to take pictures of my 2 Minature Pincshers also, Nikki and Rusty. <BR> Getting ready to change out the door hinges and Inner and outer tie-rods when the parts come in. Can't wait to feel the difference. The passenger side inner tie-rod bushing is shot ! Picked one up from Rodney, ...another good fellow to have listed in your Favorites !<P>    Thanks again everyone !!!||||reg||7
Z||000022||Zoom88||12-01-2001||08:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Toogy:<BR><B>I was just wondering if you had your car lowered at all?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well yes but no &lt;bg&gt; it has the original Springs and I am sure they have probably dropped that much LOL. Believe it or not this car had been sitting along side a shed for 5 years, been restoring it for the past 2 years. Plans are to put new springs on next spring, don't no if I will drop it or not. And I hope to have A.R.I. build me a<BR>3.4 short block next summer. Right now its a stock 2.8L , ported the Exhaust manifolds when I had them off to fix some broken manifold bolts. Replaced the stock exhaust with the Ocelot system, removed the Cat.<BR>Runs strong and sounds good, have the classic hunting idle problem though, I have replaced everything but the ECM !!<BR> Oops sorry about rambling, can't help but have a Love/Hate relationship with these little cars !!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000023||Zoom88||12-01-2001||08:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fropuff:<BR><B>Looks nice!  You have a damn nice car as well.  I was wondering about the paint.. I was wondering how much you used to paint the two scoops.  Reason I'm asking is that I need to repaint the right fender, front bumper, and rear bumper on my '92 Grand Prix.  I was wondering how much I would need.  I was thinking two cans, but it may need three?  I would only do around three coats, so it's not as many coats as you used.  Thanks.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I used a can and ahalf of the clear white<BR>and a can of clear on each one. But I don't use but 3/4 of the can because my experience with sprays has been once the pressure in the can starts to drop you risk getting uneven spray patterns and sputters. But the paint this company makes is excellent if you take your time and are patient you can spray another coat or sand between coats every twenty minutes. They have great instructions on there website.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Zoom88||12-01-2001||08:46 PM||||Hey Oreif, I have heard allot of good things about your car. I sure would Like to see some Pics. Can you direct me to some ?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||Oreif||12-01-2001||09:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Zoom88:<BR><B>Hey Oreif, I have heard allot of good things about your car. I sure would Like to see some Pics. Can you direct me to some ?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Before side scoops: (different views)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fcol_01_1.jpg"> <P>After Scoops:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Oreif_01.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000026||Zoom88||12-01-2001||09:53 PM||||Excellent, the workmanship shows !!! <BR>Tell me about that front end.<BR> I love this stuff its like, mechanical art !!||||reg||1
Z||000027||Raydar||12-02-2001||09:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sage:<BR><B>Like to remind anyone thinking about getting these, there normally is no "on hand supply" of these things.  Because of the cost of production, they are made to order.  In other words, they aren't made without an order.  We tell folks to expect a 6 - 8 week wait, but it usually doesn't take that long, we just like to prepare people and give ourselves ample time to do the job right.  Eventually we WILL get to the point that we have a small supply on hand, but we're not there yet.  Right now I have one set that could be ready to go in a days time.  I will be making a few sets in the next couple weeks, but do have some other projects in the works.  Just a little FYI.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"When you build a better mousetrap (or sidescoop) the world will beat a path to your door."<P>If my mechanical work was done, I would have already ordered a set of these. I *will* do so, sometime in the (hopefully) not too distant future. Look to be the best quality scoops I've ever seen. <P>And Zoom88 and Oreif,<BR>You guys have two of the nicest cars I've ever seen on this forum. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000028||fierohoho||12-02-2001||11:02 AM||||Zoom88, I found the site , thanks.<P>Did you take any instalation pics you could post?||||reg||1
Z||000029||Zoom88||12-02-2001||02:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>Zoom88, I found the site , thanks.<P>Did you take any instalation pics you could post?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry, I didn't take any installation Pics. Really easy though only took me about 1 1/2 hours to do both sides. Main problem I had was finding hardware to put it back together.<BR> Ended up using 6.3mm plastic rivets with a plastic rivet gun I purchased from NAPA.<BR>Rivet part #770-2870 come 20 to a pack, specify black or white. Rivet gun is 770-2864. Got the rivet idea from someone else on the forum, can't remember who though, but thanks it works great !!<BR> On the 7-8 rivets you have to drill out on the bottom of the rockers I went back with Black Plastic license plate bolts, first ones I bought where a little to short, found some longer ones at Wal-Mart. I like these for several reasons, they are easy to remove, and plastic nuts don't back off so you just need to snug them plus they look like they should have been there in the first place !!! For the trim you can get the fasteners from the Fiero Store or here<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ardeldistributors.com/category.html?UCIDs=414669%7C656537" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ardeldistributors.com/category.html?UCIDs=414669%7C656537</A> <P>Hope this helps <BR>||||reg||12
Z||000030||Zoom88||12-02-2001||02:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B> "When you build a better mousetrap (or sidescoop) the world will beat a path to your door."<P>If my mechanical work was done, I would have already ordered a set of these. I *will* do so, sometime in the (hopefully) not too distant future. Look to be the best quality scoops I've ever seen. <P>And Zoom88 and Oreif,<BR>You guys have two of the nicest cars I've ever seen on this forum. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> I have to agree with the statement about Oreif's car it is BEAUTIFUL and Unique ! <BR> Maybe we can mate the two cars and see what we come up with ... HEHE !!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000031||My7Fieros||12-03-2001||08:08 PM||||Oreif's car is incredible! I have first hand experience, seeing the car in person. Believe me, those pics dont do it justice. I'll never forget the feeling when I was at Oreif's house and he opened the garage door and pulled that thing out...my jaw hit the ground! That car is absolute PRIMO inside and out! Damn, now Im starting to drool again!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Zoom, judging by the pics you posted, your car looks to be primo as well...I cant stop looking at it! <B>PLEASE</B> post some interior pics!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo_1.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000032||Zoom88||12-04-2001||12:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Oreif's car is incredible! I have first hand experience, seeing the car in person. Believe me, those pics dont do it justice. I'll never forget the feeling when I was at Oreif's house and he opened the garage door and pulled that thing out...my jaw hit the ground! That car is absolute PRIMO inside and out! Damn, now Im starting to drool again!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Zoom, judging by the pics you posted, your car looks to be primo as well...I cant stop looking at it! [b]PLEASE</B> post some interior pics!<P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Thanks, I'll try and post some interior pics first chance I get.<P>||||reg||1
